\par\par \b \uc2 TECHNICALS- \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  market views and key levels.  \b0\par\par\uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2004\par 17:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     NEW YORK, Jan 29 (Reuters) - Following is a selection of\par comments from analysts on important technical developments in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     TECHNICAL ANALYSIS TEAM, CREDIT SUISSE FIRST BOSTON\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -EURO/DOLLAR: "Our short-term outlook remains  \f28 \par \par \uc2 sideways/bearish as prices closed well below the 13-day moving  \par \par \uc2 average at $1.2578, the 50 percent retracement of $1.2555 and  \par \par \uc2 the 61.8 percent retracement of $1.2505 at $1.2475. The daily  \par \par \uc2 momentum chart has turned neutral below the 50 percent level,  \par \par \uc2 while a weak close on Tuesday below $1.2445 would turn that  \par \par \uc2 oscillator to the downside, signaling that weakness should  \par \par \uc2 easily challenge the $1.2334 low ahead of the $1.2200 zone.  \par \par \uc2 "Resistance shifts to $1.2540 and $1.2575, but it will take  \par \par \uc2 a close back above $1.2640 just to steady this break. A close  \par \par \uc2 back to last week's high at $1.2775 is needed to test the  \par \par \uc2 $1.2900 high - itself a major upside breakout point."  \par \par \uc2 -DOLLAR/SWISS FRANC: "Our short-term outlook remains  \par \par \uc2 sideways/bullish, as prices held above the 1.2400 franc support  \par \par \uc2 and finally closed back above the 1.2445 franc 13-day moving  \par \par \uc2 average to register a five-day high close at 1.2545 francs.  \par \par \uc2 This strength should offer the 1.2565-1.2585 francs and  \par \par \uc2 1.2610-1.2630 franc resistance into Wednesday followed by the  \par \par \uc2 top of this month's 1.2140-1.2725 franc range.  \par \par \uc2 "The big surprise now will be to see this market not only  \par \par \uc2 close above the 1.2725 franc high but above the 1.2775-1.2800  \par \par \uc2 franc weekly "breakout" zone to suggest that a move into the  \par \par \uc2 1.3200 franc area is a probability in what could see a wide  \par \par \uc2 trading range unfold. Support shifts to 1.2515 francs, but  \par \par \uc2 holding above 1.2475-1.2460 will be essential for the upside to  \par \par \uc2 continue to develop as the daily momentum chart turns up from a  \par \par \uc2 mid-range level - a bullish sign for even more advancement. A  \par \par \uc2 close below the 1.2360-1.2345 zone would negate this recovery  \par \par \uc2 to retest last week's low at 1.2275 francs, ahead of the 1.2140  \par \par \uc2 franc low."  \par \par \uc2 TECHNICAL ANALYSIS TEAM, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  CONCEPTS:  \par \par \uc2 -EURO/DOLLAR: "A break below $1.2420 calls for a slide to  \par \par \uc2 the pivotal $1.2333 level. Further support lies at $1.2316 from  \par \par \uc2 the 38.2 percent Fibonacci retracement level of the November  \par \par \uc2 January uptrend. A drop to $1.2154 remains very unlikely. Above  \par \par \uc2 $1.2550, the euro/dollar has resistance at around $1.2620 and  \par \par \uc2 then at a distant $1.2774. A break above this level signals  \par \par \uc2 that the euro/dollar has resuming its rally and it will tackle  \par \par \uc2 the pivotal resistance at 1.$2895. Oscillators are now edging  \par \par \uc2 lower."  \par \par \uc2 -DOLLAR/YEN: "Continues to remain weak overall, in spite  \par \par \uc2 of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and will remain weak for  \par \par \uc2 as long as the resistance of the declining 20-day moving  \par \par \uc2 average holds. Pivotal support remains at 105.45 yen. However,  \par \par \uc2 strong support continues to be found at 105.60 yen from a  \par \par \uc2 50-point pivot that targets 105.10 yen and 106.10 yen. Strong  \par \par \uc2 resistance remains from the 50-point pivot at 106.75 yen, which  \par \par \uc2 targets 106.25 yen and 107.25 yen. Further resistance is at  \par \par \uc2 107.51 yen. Oscillators are mixed."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 11:30 a.m. EST (16:30 GMT). All data  \par \par \uc2 taken from Reuters calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m.  \par \par \uc2 (21:30 GMT) in the previous New York session.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Last  US Close   %      YTD      2003\par                              28 Jan.   Change %Change  Close\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.2390   1.2480   -0.72   -1.49   1.2578\par Dlr/yen              106.07   106.12   -0.05   -1.16   107.31\par Euro/yen             131.42   132.45   -0.78   -2.67   135.03\par Dlr/swiss            1.2599   1.2554   +0.36   +1.58   1.2403\par Stg/dlr              1.8137   1.8209   -0.40   +1.61   1.7850\par Dlr/cad              1.3348   1.3253   +0.72   +2.95   1.2965\par Aus/dlr              0.7607   0.7729   -1.58   +1.21   0.7516\par Euro/swiss           1.5614   1.5661   -0.30   +0.10   1.5599\par Euro/stg             0.6829   0.6849   -0.29   -3.07   0.7045\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All spots  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo spots  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe spots  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volatilities  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par  Economic Forecasts...          Official rates...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par  Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par  Press Digests....         Polls on 