\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-BOJ may yet surprise with  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  move near G7 meet.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada   \par \uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2004\par 06:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 29 (Reuters) - Those who thought \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had backtracked on its policy of massive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid criticism at an upcoming meeting of Group of Seven (G7) countries may have been wrong.   \par \par \uc2 Unlike at the time of the previous G7 gathering held in Dubai in September, Japanese authorities will most likely maintain their presence in the market before and after the February 6-7 meeting and step in whenever the yen strengthens, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 Some players who thought \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was easing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance ahead of the Florida meeting were caught off guard by a suspected Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday that briefly pushed the dollar up more than one yen.   \par \par \uc2 "I think they learned a lesson from Dubai that if they don't act during G7, they will have to spend more money on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when they resume," said Hideo Kumano, a senior economist at Dai-ichi Life Research Institute.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  between September 16 and 30 - before and after the September 20 Dubai meeting.   \par \par \uc2 On September 30, when the BOJ finally stepped in after allowing the dollar to fall sharply to 111 yen from around 117 yen, it sold a massive 1.06 trillion yen ($9.98 billion).   \par \par \uc2 In 2003, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record 20 trillion yen in yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and analysts expect it to have spent around six trillion yen so far this month. January \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures were to be released on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 ECB AND BOJ   \par \par \uc2 But speculation that Tokyo may temporarily loosen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy surfaced on Tuesday after Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at smoothing volatility, not at keeping the yen at a certain level.   \par \par \uc2 The comments were taken by traders as a sign the MOF would refrain from aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be unwelcome to European officials, who could see it as an additional reason for the euro's appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 Speculation that there would be no Japanese action drove the yen to a three-year high of 105.45 yen per dollar on Tuesday and prompted the BOJ to take action the following day. MOF officials have reiterated that Tanigaki's remarks on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not represent a policy change.   \par \par \uc2 In contrast, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) officials have only recently started to verbally warn against the euro's steep 15 percent rise against the dollar since the Dubai meeting. The yen has only risen about nine percent versus the dollar during that period.   \par \par \uc2 Many analysts think ECB officials would turn to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only as a last resort in halting the euro's rise.   \par \par \uc2 The last time the ECB stepped into the market was in November 2000, after a series of interest rate rises and an internationally coordinated mission to support the euro failed to stop it falling to record lows of around $0.8225.   \par \par \uc2 Some analysts therefore see last week's surprise monetary easing by the BOJ as having more political than financial significance.   \par \par \uc2 "Japanese officials don't want to be seen as making efforts only in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring up the economy. They needed the BOJ to ease to show that they are doing more," said Takashi Yamanaka, an economist at UFJ Bank.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to raise the target for excess liquidity it supplies to the money market, raising the target band for banks' current account deposits parked at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 30-35 trillion yen from 27-32 trillion yen. ($1=106.18 Yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040129e01t00dls\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
