\par\par \b \uc2 SCHEDULE-Asia Business News at 0520 GMT.   \b0\par\par\uc2 926 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2004\par 06:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Editor: Christopher Kaufman\par     Telephone: +65 6870-3852\par     All times GMT.\par     TOP STORIES:\par     SINGPAPORE - Stock, bond markets spooked by Fed\par     WELLINGTON - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprises with rate hike\par     TOKYO - Electronics demand sparks jump in industrial\par output. HONG KONG - Hutch sells Hong Kong phone business to\par Vanda\par     - - - -\par     SINGAPORE - Stocks and bonds sink and the dollar steadies\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 after an unexpected change in the U.S. Federal Reserve's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 message to the markets suggests the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be a step   \par \par \uc2 closer to raising interest rates. (MARKETS-GLOBAL (WRAPUP 1),   \par \par \uc2 expect by 0730, by Christopher Kaufman, 750 words)   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON - New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprises investors   \par \par \uc2 with a 25 basis point rate hike, saying it needs to check   \par \par \uc2 pressure on prices from consumer spending, construction and a   \par \par \uc2 hot housing market. (ECONOMY-NEWZEALAND-RATES (UPDATE 2), moved   \par \par \uc2 at 0438, by Miranda Maxwell, 700 words)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO - Japan's industrial output rose strongly in the   \par \par \uc2 final quarter of last year, spurred by demand for electronics   \par \par \uc2 goods, with a slight drop in December unlikely to knock the   \par \par \uc2 country's economic recovery off track. (ECONOMY-JAPAN-OUTPUT   \par \par \uc2 (UPDATE 3), expect by 0700, by Jonathan Standing, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG - Li Ka-shing's Hutchison Whampoa sells its Hong Kong   \par \par \uc2 fixed-line phone business to Vanda Systems, an affiliated firm,   \par \par \uc2 for $910 million in a deal that sends Vanda shares soaring.   \par \par \uc2 (TELECOMS-HONGKONG-HUTCHISON (UPDATE 3), expect by 0700, by   \par \par \uc2 Tony Munroe, 600 words)    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - - - -\par     COMPANIES\par     AUCKLAND - New Zealand's biggest wood products firm Carter\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Holt Harvey posts a five percent fall in fourth-quarter   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 operating profit as revenues remain flat, but says it expects   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 domestic markets to stay strong. (TIMBER-NEWZEALAND-CARTERHOLT   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (UPDATE 2), expect by 0500, by James Gray, 600 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE - ST Assembly Test Services Ltd, the world's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fifth-largest tester of microchips, posts stronger quarterly   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 profit thanks to robust wireless demand, and forecast five   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent rise in first-quarter sales. (TECH-STASSEMBLY-EARNS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (UPDATE 2), moved at 0350, by Jennifer Tan, 640 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO - Nissan Motor and Mazda Motor are expected to kick   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 off the third-quarter earnings season for Japan's top auto   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 makers with solid sales numbers that should put them on track   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to post rosy full-year profits. (AUTOS-JAPAN-EARNINGS (UPDATE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2), expect by 0830, by Chang-Ran Kim, 700 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO - Nomura Holdings and other top Japanese brokerages   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 are expected to report a steep upturn in quarterly earnings,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 propelled by active equity financing that brought a surge in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fees. (FINANCIAL-JAPAN-BROKERAGE (UPDATE 2), expect by 0830, by   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Miki Shimogori, 700 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 