s. (TELECOMS-KOREA-KT-PREVIEW,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 moved at 0429, by Kim Miyoung, 650 words)    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - - - -\par     MARKETS/ECONOMY\par     TOKYO - Those who thought \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had stepped back from its\par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy out of fear of coming   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 under fire at an upcoming Group of Seven (G7) meeting may have   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 second thoughts after what seems to have been another foray   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this week. (MARKETS-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (ANALYSIS), expect by   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0800, by Kazunori Takada, 650 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KYOTO, Japan - Bank of Japan Policy Board member Teizo Taya   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 says the impact of the yen's rise on exports has so far been   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 limited, although the global effects of a weaker dollar need   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 watching. (ECONOMY-JAPAN-BOJ-TAYA (UPDATE 1), expect by 0700,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by Chisa Fujioka, 500 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE - Asia will grow robustly in 2004 as the region's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 export engine benefits from improving global conditions,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 signalling a possible end to deflation in some economies, the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 latest Reuters poll of regional analysts shows.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (ECONOMY-ASIA-POLL (WRAPUP 1), moving shortly, by John Mair,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 750 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL - South Korean consumer inflation is expected to have   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 risen in January on higher prices of food and industrial goods,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 but analysts said they do not see it to be enough to force the   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rethink its interest rate policy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (ECONOMY-KOREA-CPI (POLL), expect by 0600, by Oh Jung-hwa, 550   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MANILA - The Philippine economy kept up a mild recovery in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the last quarter of 2003, expanding 1.6 percent as steady farm   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 output and ever-dependable consumers helped sustain a year of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 modest growth (ECONOMY-PHILIPPINES (UPDATE 3), expect by 0830,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by Dolly Aglay, 600 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040129e01t00di6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
