\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar firms on Fed statement, but gains seen limited.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Chikafumi Hodo  \par \uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2004\par 02:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 29 (Reuters) - The dollar firmed on Thursday as an unexpected change in the wording of the U.S. Federal Reserve's statement after its policy-setting meeting suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be a step closer to raising interest rates.   \par \par \uc2  The greenback posted broad-based gains on active short-covering after the Fed dropped the phrase referring to a "considerable period" of loose monetary policy from its statement, while keeping its interest rates unchanged.   \par \par \uc2  But active follow-through sales were limited as the market was careful about holding on to large dollar-long positions before the Group of Seven (G7) industrial powers meet next week, traders said.   \par \par \uc2  "The Fed's statement surprised the market at a time when the focus has been on the G7 meeting," said Hideaki Furumaya, head of the corporate desk at Trust and Custody Services Bank.   \par \par \uc2  "But it's premature to become too bullish on the dollar as the market really doesn't expect the credit tightening to happen very soon," he said.   \par \par \uc2  The euro lost ground against the dollar and the yen in early Asian trade as active stop-loss selling, triggered around $1.2440, briefly sent the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a low of $1.2416.   \par \par \uc2  But it found firm support after hitting the low.   \par \par \uc2  At 0033 GMT, the euro stood at $1.2458/63 against the late U.S. level of $1.2480/85.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar hovered just above 106 yen steady from the late-U.S. level but up from the overnight low near 105.50.   \par \par \uc2  Its topside was blocked by heavy sell orders rumoured to be lined up above 106.40 yen, traders said.   \par \par \uc2  "The perception that there is strong selling interest in the dollar/yen rate really hasn't changed," Furumaya said.   \par \par \uc2  Traders said yen-buying demand in the cross market was also putting downward pressure on the dollar/yen rate.   \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 132.08/18 yen after dropping as low as 131.82 yen earlier in the morning.   \par \par \uc2  Traders said that Japanese institutions, such as life insurers, were eagerly looking for chances to lock in profits in euro/yen ahead of fiscal book closings at the end of March.   \par \par \uc2  But the market was careful about buying the yen too aggressively amid persistent wariness that Japan might step into the market to sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.   \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Japanese authorities were seen buying dollars against the yen, trying to stem the renewed uptrend of the yen, which had intensified on market doubts about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commitment to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Thursday that stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets over the medium term were desirable and that the authorities were closely monitoring the market.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040129e01t0039v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
