\par\par \b \uc2 Asset flows to Japan show no respite for yen gains.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez   \par \uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2004\par 21:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 28 (Reuters) - Those betting on a slowdown in the yen's rise, thinking the Bank of Japan could stem the tide of hefty inflows into the world's second-largest economy, might want to think again.   \par \par \uc2 Capital flows into yen assets tracked by big U.S. banks show continued foreign buying of Japanese assets in January, easily outstripping offshore interest in U.S. or Euro zone investments.   \par \par \uc2 This suggests further strength in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar despite intensive efforts by the Bank of Japan to curb its strength, analysts say. The BoJ, which acts on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has routinely undertaken yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak in an attempt to aid exporters.   \par \par \uc2 "Our momentum indicator suggests that the yen could see more buying, particularly against the dollar," said Karin Kimbrough, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Morgan Stanley in New York, citing the bank's proprietary flows data.   \par \par \uc2 By contrast, buying momentum in the once red-hot euro has tapered off, which should temporarily halt the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance against the dollar, Kimbrough said.   \par \par \uc2 JP Morgan's Flow of Funds data also show the same trend - fairly substantial foreign buying of Japanese stocks. Based on the bank's recent data, flows into Japanese equities are still roughly in line with last year's average inflows.   \par \par \uc2 By contrast, there were net equity outflows from Europe. They were slightly larger than last year's average outflow, while capital flows into the United States were flat.   \par \par \uc2 "Positions, valuation, and economic strength seem to suggest an even stronger yen," said Rebecca Patterson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan in New York.   \par \par \uc2 She said Japan's export and capital expenditure-driven recovery is on track and the yen's strength does not seem to be undermining it.   \par \par \uc2 Driven by vigorous exports and capital spending, real economic growth in the last three months of 2003 is widely expected to have grown considerably more than the 1.4 percent expansion achieved in the previous quarter, analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 MONEY FLOWS INTO JAPAN, YEN STRENGTH   \par \par \uc2 The trend in U.S. banks' private flows data is also consistent with portfolio investments monitored by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . According to the latest MoF data, portfolio investments of about $20 billion in the week ending Jan. 16 represented the largest net inflow on record, dating back to the week of March 10, 1999, according to Bank of New York's senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Michael Woolfolk.   \par \par \uc2 "Money is flowing heavily into \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is overwhelming the dollar-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Andrew Busch, global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BMO Nesbitt Burns in Chicago.   \par \par \uc2 Although most analysts do not expect the BoJ to stand aside and allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen at the expense of Japan's exporters, some believe the BoJ can afford to relax for a bit and allow a marginal rise in the yen without undermining Japan's recovery.   \par \par \uc2 While the dollar has fallen sharply against the yen in the last year and the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is inching toward highs last seen in 1999-2000, the yen on a wider scale has not appreciated as much as other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is still well below its previous peaks, analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 Since the Group of Seven meeting of industrial nations in Dubai in September, the yen rose around 5 percent in real inflation-adjusted terms, and around 9.5 percent against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 But the real effective exchange rate, a measure of price competitiveness vis-a-vis other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is still around 15 percent lower than its peaks, RBC Capital said in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have tempered the damage of a rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the economy by preventing the yen from climbing as much as the euro and some other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Japan spent 20 trillion yen ($190 billion) in huge dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003, which traders suspect have continued this year.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040128e01s003hp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
