\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar drops on soft US data.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Manuela Badawy  \par \uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2004\par 19:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 27 (Reuters) - The dollar fell more than 1 percent against the euro and Swiss franc and notched a three-year low against the yen on Tuesday as signs of labor market softness in a U.S. consumer confidence report surprised traders.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback was already under pressure from better-than-expected European data and comments from one Japanese policy-maker who said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at smoothing the yen's volatility, not to stop its ascent.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer confidence improved in January but Americans were still having a tough time finding jobs, the Conference Board said. Its index of confidence jumped to 96.8 in January from a revised 91.7 in December.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts had forecast a rise to 96.3, but traders said the market expected an even better report and as a result sold the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "It is consistent with a U.S. economy continuing to gain ground in the first half of the year. But at the margin, it is disappointing relative to expectations," said Tim Stewart, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "There is so much event risk coming up with the G7 meeting that any individual number is not going to provide a major dislocation to pricing. I think that is true of this number today," he said.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Early on Tuesday afternoon in New York, the euro  rose 1.2 percent on\par the day to $1.2620 according to Reuters data, while the Australian\par dollar rose 1.1 percent versus the greenback to $0.7780      .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar lost 1.27 percent against the Swiss franc to trade around 1.2410 francs .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market had bought quite a few dollars back in the last few days and it didn't find a solid reason to continue that process," said Robert Sinche, global head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at Citibank in New York.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The euro tested and held - in the short-term - some trend line support that came in this morning to $1.2425. So when it went down and tested that support and held it, the market started buying back euros, and then it just got its own momentum," Sinche added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell below a three-year low of 105.70 yen set in January, pressured by speculation that Japan would limit its sales of yen before the Feb. 6-7 meeting of Group of Seven industrial nations finance ministers in Florida.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "On the yen, (the rise) is a separate issue. We have seen the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  back away from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prior to major meetings and that may be something the market is focusing on," Sinche added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen firmed against the dollar after Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Tuesday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market was aimed at smoothing volatility and not at keeping the yen at a certain level.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is aimed at removing volatility from the market," Tanigaki said in response to parliamentary questions. "We don't use it to keep the yen at a certain level or lead the yen lower."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar traded at 105.69 yen, down 0.56 percent on the day, just above a three-year low of 105.63 yen hit earlier, according to Reuters data.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sterling rose to $1.8254, up 0.65 percent. British Prime Minister Tony Blair faced potentially the most perilous 48 hours of his premiership over a probe of the suicide of a top British expert on Iraqi weapons.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A stronger-than-expected German business confidence index helped the euro rise against the dollar in European trade.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The influential German Ifo economic research institute, which polls about 7,000 firms each month, said its index rose to 97.4 in January, the highest since January 2001, from an upwardly revised 96.9 in December.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Open Market Committee's two-day policy meeting started on Tuesday. With no interest rate change expected, the market is waiting to see whether the Fed's statement drops a reference to rates remaining on hold for a "considerable period."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Daniel Bases in New York contributed to this report).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040127e01r003mp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
