\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Sinks As Exporters Sell; MOF Bids Support  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 894 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2004\par 06:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell against the yen in Asia Monday under persistent selling pressure from Japanese exporters, although bidding by Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities once again stemmed the fall, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit fell more than half a yen as many export firms stepped up sales after revising down their in-house exchange rate targets for the coming months, a surge dealers say could last a week or more.  \par \par \uc2 Most companies project exchange rates for the fiscal year from April around the beginning of the calendar year. A survey of exporters reported by the Nihon Keizai Shimbun Monday found many now forecast the dollar will trade between Y100 and Y105 in fiscal 2004.  \par \par \uc2 That compares with their previous target range around Y110 or above for many companies.  \par \par \uc2 "A lot of exporters hashed out their plans last week, and we're starting to see them executed," a Tokyo brokerage dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro also sank against the yen, dragged down by the dollar's slide as well as some direct exporter selling, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit's fall came to a halt at a familiar level, however, as bids thought to originate from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities acted as a safety net around Y106.10.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has defended that level consistently this month, generally placing covert bids through commercial banks, although the dollar has fallen below Y106 several times.  \par \par \uc2 On those occasions, including the dollar's tumble to a three-year low of Y105.71 Jan. 16, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , acting on the Finance Ministry's orders, has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively to push it back up.  \par \par \uc2 Traders estimate the BOJ has spent around Y7 trillion this month all told on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - already more than a third of the record Y20.05 trillion it spent in all of last year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts have made many would-be sellers wary of jumping on official-looking bids, lest they trigger a fresh round of full-blown \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "People are hesitating to hit the bids aggressively," the brokerage dealer said. "That's putting a floor under the dollar as much as the bids themselves."  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y106.10, below Y106.67 in early trade and Y106.57 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at Y106.17 late Friday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2574, lower than $1.2589 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.2703 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y133.44, down from Y134.19 in early trade but up from Y133.19 in New York late Friday. The euro was at Y134.86 in Tokyo late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8263, steady from $1.8265 in New York but lower than $1.8426 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Trade data released Monday showed Japan's booming trade with Asia is more than compensating for the strong yen's chilling effect on U.S.-bound exports.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's merchandise trade surplus rose 3.6% to Y10.239 trillion in 2003 for a second straight year of growth, the Finance Ministry said.  \par \par \uc2 In December alone, the trade surplus expanded 41.2% from a year earlier to Y1.122 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the yen's steady rise toward the end of last year, exports grew 8.5% in December, helping full-year exports rise 4.7%. Imports grew 1.6% in December and expanded 5.0% during the full calendar year.  \par \par \uc2 While Japan's trade surplus with the U.S. fell 11.2% in December to Y558.8 billion, its trade with Asia produced a surplus of Y722.0 billion, up 52.4%.  \par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, technical analysis showed Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped form horizontal trendline support for the dollar just above Y105.70.  \par \par \uc2 Continued exporter selling and market jitters ahead of the Feb. 6-7 Group of Seven meeting in Boca Raton, Florida could threaten that support, although a thicket of options-related barriers from just below that level to around Y104 could mitigate any further fall.  \par \par \uc2 "It's very congested in that zone," a Tokyo dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's advance Monday came despite a weekend report that Japanese bank regulators suspect one of the country's biggest banks may have hidden pessimistic loan assessments from government inspectors.  \par \par \uc2 The Financial Services Agency plans to start inspecting UFJ Banks' loan-related records as early as this month, The Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported in its Saturday morning edition.  \par \par \uc2 The highly unusual action follows the discovery of documents showing that the actual evaluations of many borrowers' financial situations were worse than the assessments contained in the official documents that the bank showed to the agency.  \par \par \uc2 UFJ said it hadn't heard from the FSA about any such inspection.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson and Bennett Richardson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040126e01q00047\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
