\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED -  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar up vs some rivals, eyeing US, Europe stance.   \b0\par\par\uc2 919 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2004\par 19:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 In NEW YORK story "\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Dollar up vs some rivals, eyeing US, Europe stance" please delete paragraph 3 which misinterpreted comments by U.S. Undersecretary of Trade Grant Aldonas, and narrative in first and second paragraphs referring to U.S. official's comments.   \par \par \uc2 A corrected version follows. (Updates prices, adds analyst comment, U.S. data, European official comments)   \par \par \uc2 By Manuela Badawy   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 26 (Reuters) - The dollar gained against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday following European talk about curbing euro strength ahead of next week's meeting of finance ministers from the Group of Seven industrial nations.   \par \par \uc2 European politicians expressed mixed opinions on the need for action to curb volatile exchange rates.   \par \par \uc2 "One of the reasons for the choppiness today is because of a fairly steady stream of comments coming out of the euro zone on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Nick Bennenbroek, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Brown Brothers Harriman & Co. in New York.   \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied French Finance Minister Francis Mer's weekend comment that ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet discussed interest rates in a meeting with euro zone finance ministers last week, sending the euro briefly higher.   \par \par \uc2 "I don't think markets are particularly active. The market is focusing more on these (politicians') comments than they would do otherwise simply because there is nothing going on and because the markets are a little thin," Bennenbroek said.   \par \par \uc2 Early Monday in New York, the euro was trading a tad softer against the dollar to $1.2550 .   \par \par \uc2 The dollar weakened against the yen on Monday after the Japanese Finance Ministry reported that its trade surplus expanded for the fifth time in six months in December and on commercial selling and exporters' demand for yen.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to 106.08 yen, shedding half a percent. The yen scored three-year highs against the dollar just beyond 106 earlier this month.   \par \par \uc2 The head of Japan's largest business lobby said on Monday that he hoped the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the dollar fell below 105 yen because most companies have said their assumed dollar/yen rate is 105 to 110 yen.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar was unaffected by the rise in sales of existing U.S. homes. Sales rose in December by 6.9 percent, according to data released by the National Association of Realtors on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Sales of previously owned homes rose to a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 6.47 million units from a revised 6.05 million in November.   \par \par \uc2 "It doesn't look like the dollar moved very much," said Carl Weinberg, chief economist at High Frequency Economics.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is on hold waiting for confirmation tomorrow about the FOMC and see what changes that bring. The market is on hold mode for the ECB next week and the G7 the week after," Weinberg said.   \par \par \uc2 WHAT TO SAY?   \par \par \uc2 European officials seemed to give conflicting statements regarding the dollar's need to strengthen to prevent a crisis but not at their expense or too rapidly.   \par \par \uc2 G7 finance officials, known as sherpas, gathered in Brussels on Monday as part of a wider meeting of G10 officials and academics.   \par \par \uc2 The Irish Finance Minister Charlie McCreevy said in a statement for delivery before a European Parliament committee: "It was made clear by Eurogroup Ministers and the ECB that our long-term strategy does not change: the euro must keep its value over the medium-and long run, in line with economic fundamentals."   \par \par \uc2 McCreevy as well as Dutch Finance Minister Gerrit Zalm stressed on stability and showed concern over excessive exchange rate moves.   \par \par \uc2 Spain's Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said an abrupt \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market correction could be dangerous but that a strong and stable euro was useful for the euro zone economy.   \par \par \uc2 The market is also keenly awaiting a two-day Federal Open Market Committee meeting starting on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Although the U.S. Federal Reserve is not expected to change its monetary policy, traders will scrutinize the wording of the statement it issues after the meeting on Wednesday for clues on whether the Fed may hike rates later in the year.   \par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan is expected to take part via videolink in a conference in London hosted by UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 11:08 a.m. EST (16:08 GMT). All data\par taken from Reuters calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m.\par (21:30 GMT) in the previous New York session.\par  \par                       Last  US Close    %      YTD     2003\par                              23 Jan.  Change %Change    Close\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.2555   1.2585   -0.24   -0.18   1.2578\par Dlr/yen              106.10   106.62   -0.49   -1.13   107.31\par Euro/yen             133.20   134.17   -0.72   -1.36   135.03\par Dlr/swiss            1.2473   1.2422   +0.41   +0.56   1.2403\par Stg/dlr              1.8185   1.8259   -0.41   +1.88   1.7850\par Dlr/cad              1.3118   1.3130   -0.09   +1.18   1.2965\par Aus/dlr              0.7733   0.7722   +0.14   +2.89   0.7516\par Euro/swiss           1.5663   1.5631   +0.20   +0.41   1.5599\par Euro/stg             0.6901   0.6890   +0.16   -2.04   0.7045\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All spots   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo spots   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe spots   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volatilities   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par  Economic Forecasts...          Official rates...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par  Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par  Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par  European markets......\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040126e01q0054b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
