\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steadies versus euro as G7 positions eyed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2004\par 10:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 26 (Reuters) - The dollar steadied against the euro but fell back towards recent three-year lows against the yen on Monday as traders debated how the Group of Seven would react to the greenback's recent weakness.  \par \par \uc2 Deputy ministers from the G7 club of industrialised nations meet in Brussels later on Monday in preparation for a finance ministers' meeting to be held in Florida on February 6-7. With the euro up 40 percent against the dollar in two years, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are expected to be high on the agenda.  \par \par \uc2 The euro stood at $1.2695 at 0900 GMT, having recovered from an early bout of weakness to stand little changed on the day. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit record highs near $1.29 two weeks ago.  \par \par \uc2 "There are significant risks to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions in the coming weeks which may be making the market more choppy," said Marvin Barth, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Citibank.  \par \par \uc2 "People are still trying to figure out what the comments on the euro mean."  \par \par \uc2 Speaking in Davos on Saturday, French Finance Minister Francis Mer said euro zone finance ministers, worried at the strength of the euro, had discussed an interest rate cut with the head of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week.  \par \par \uc2 But ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet gave little sign that a rate cut was pending, saying there was plenty of cheap money in the euro zone. A top International Monetary Fund official said neither euro zone rate cuts nor \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were needed right now.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Undersecretary for Trade Grant Aldonas said in Paris on Monday the forthcoming G7 meeting should focus economic fundamentals more than on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, reinforcing the market view that Washington is comfortable with a weaker dollar.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  SURPLUS DWARFED BY \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The dollar was down half a percent at 106.10 yen , moving back within sight of three-year lows around 105.70 hit earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback had a volatile session against the yen on Friday with dealers suspecting Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars to prevent a break to new three-year lows.  \par \par \uc2 The market showed little reaction to Finance Ministry figures showing Japan's trade surplus rose 41.2 percent in December from a year earlier, with exports rising 8.5 percent and imports gaining 1.6 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's persistent trade surplus has often been cited as a reason behind the yen's strength. But the surplus for the whole of calendar 2003 was only about half of the roughly 20 trillion yen that Japanese authorities spent on yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the year.  \par \par \uc2 FOMC AWAITED  \par \par \uc2 The market was keenly awaiting a two-day Federal Open Market Committee meeting starting on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Although the U.S. Federal Reserve is not expected to change its monetary policy for now, traders will scrutinise the wording of the statement for clues on whether the Fed may hike rates later in the year.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. fourth-quarter growth figures are also due this week and are likely to show the world's biggest economy continued to expand strongly, though probably not at the breakneck pace of 8.2 percent seen in the previous quarter.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040126e01q0027q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
