\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro drops after potential euro zone warning.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases  \par \uc2 722 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2004\par 18:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, new throughout, changes byline, changes dateline, previous LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 23 (Reuters) - The euro extended its decline against the dollar on Friday after a diplomatic source told Reuters that euro zone ministers attending a Group of Seven meeting next month will say further strength in the euro could cause the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The European diplomatic source told Reuters in London that current euro zone monetary policy supports growth, but that external shocks, including those coming from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, could reduce growth.  \par \par \uc2 "This does not mean that monetary policy reacts directly to exchange rates but rather to the effects of exchange rates on growth and inflation," the source told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 Uppermost in the market's thoughts is what G7 industrial nations' finance ministers will say about dollar weakness when they meet in Florida on Feb. 6-7.  \par \par \uc2 Before the comments, the euro was already lower against the dollar as investors took profits on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp rise earlier in the week.  \par \par \uc2 "The euro fell on these Reuters headlines. The suggestion that the ECB is nearing a place at which it would say that further appreciation of the euro from current levels would be enough to trigger a monetary policy reaction is significant for the exchange rate," said Jason Bonanca, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "If the ECB turns to a more dovish tone, that means there is less of a divergence with the Fed, meaning the ECB is willing to do a little reflation of their own, and that would be bad for the euro against the dollar," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell from around $1.2685 after the comments to a session low $1.2615, a loss of 0.7 percent from Thursday's New York close.  \par \par \uc2 MIXED SIGNALS  \par \par \uc2 Even as the euro suffered a sell-off, it is still up 3 cents against the dollar this week.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the roller-coaster ride for the euro over the last few weeks, which saw it drop five cents from a record high near $1.29 on Jan. 12, is caused by mixed signals coming from euro zone policy makers.  \par \par \uc2 "After three weeks of European officials' comments, they wanted to at least halt the precipitous slide of the dollar and were successful, but they are sending mixed signals to the market about euro/dollar strength," said Joe Francomano, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Erste Bank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "They say they do not favor such volatile and quick drops in the dollar as we have seen over the past two months, however they signaled they can live with a strong euro," he said.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Otmar Issing reiterated on Thursday the bank's worries about sharp movements in the euro.  \par \par \uc2 He noted in an interview with Reuters on Friday that tax increases and one-off factors would push euro zone inflation up 0.3 percent in early 2004 but euro strength would dampen price gains.  \par \par \uc2 ECB policymakers have stopped short of mapping out how they would reduce volatility and curb euro strength, with no strong indication they would use interest rates or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an option.  \par \par \uc2 "There is certainly a pain threshold, but I think it is more about the pace of decline rather than a specific level the ECB is thinking about. I think we are butting up against it at about 20 percent a year," said Michael Woolfolk, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New York.  \par \par \uc2 Issing and ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet are both due to speak at the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland again later on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 French Finance Minister Francis Mer said in Davos on Friday that the strong euro is starting to hurt corporate profits and may dent business confidence in Europe.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose slightly to 106.10 yen on the day and recovered from a near three-year low of 105.76 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The market remains on guard for possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell to 133.88 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose 1 percent against the Canadian dollar to C$1.3081 on expectations of further rate cuts in Canada, following a quarter-point cut this week.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040123e01n0050w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
