\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar stays on downward path vs euro, up vs yen.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada   \par \uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2004\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 23 (Reuters) - The dollar drifted down to near one-week lows against the euro on Friday, but it managed to squeeze out gains against the yen on ever-present wariness that Japan would step in to prop up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "At these levels, you have to be cautious about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at UFJ Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent 20 trillion yen ($188.6 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help support an export-led economic recovery, and market players estimate it has offloaded another six trillion so far in 2004.   \par \par \uc2 "I think 105 yen is the defence line for Japanese authorities now but they are taking a one yen buffer," said Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.   \par \par \uc2 By 0244 GMT, the dollar was up at 106.20/23 yen versus 106.03/11 in late U.S. trade. Traders said buying by Japanese importers was also lending a hand to the greenback.   \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the dollar fell to a one-week low of 105.94 yen, just short of a three-year low of 105.70.   \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, reiterated on Friday his standard line that Japanese authorities were continuing to watch movements in the markets closely.   \par \par \uc2 The euro was moving up to $1.2727/34, slightly below a one-week high of $1.2752 hit the previous day but still up from 1.2710/16 in late New York.   \par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a life high near $1.29 last week.   \par \par \uc2 "It is true that European officials have been voicing concerns about the euro's strength, so I think it won't be able to test new highs at least until after the G7 (Group of Seven meeting)" said a trader at a major Japanese bank.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar started slipping on Thursday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB), in its monthly bulletin, voiced concerns about large swings in exchange rates. Some traders had expected the ECB to send out a stronger warning.   \par \par \uc2 ECB Chief Economist Otmar Issing also reiterated on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's worries about sharp movements in the euro.   \par \par \uc2 "We hold with our concern about the brutality" of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, he told reporters before addressing a dinner discussing global economic convergence sponsored by the World Economic Forum annual meeting in Davos, Switzerland.   \par \par \uc2 With the dollar's weakness widely expected to be a topic at the February 6-7 G7 meeting in Florida, the market was expected to keep an eye out for any hints of a G7 statement or action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Sherpas from the G7 economic powers are due to meet in Brussels on Monday for preliminary talks known as G7D.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki told a news conference he hoped to give an accurate picture of Japan's fiscal and monetary policies at the G7 meeting. ($1=106.05 yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040123e01n000xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
