\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar bounces vs yen as BOJ wariness grows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Shinichi Kishima  \par \uc2 451 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2004\par 02:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 23 (Reuters) - The dollar inched up against the yen on Friday as traders became increasingly wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to a hair's breadth of last week's three-year lows.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's renewed broad-based decline this week brought it within a quarter yen of last week's 105.70 yen trough late on Thursday, keeping the market on alert for yen-selling by Japanese authorities.  \par \par \uc2 "At these levels, you have to be cautious about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at UFJ Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent 20 trillion yen ($188.6 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and market players estimate it has already offloaded another six trillion in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 With the dollar's weakness widely expected to be a topic at the February 6-7 Group of Seven meeting in Florida, the market was likely to remain very cautious in the near term about any hints of a possible G7 statement or action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Sherpas from the G7 economic powers are due to meet in Brussels on Monday for preliminary talks known as G7D.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to around 106.23/26 yen by 0057 GMT, up about a quarter yen on the day.  \par \par \uc2 It was little changed against the euro at around $1.2715 to the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but traders said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked groggy after retracing about two-thirds of the ground it had recovered from last week's life lows near $1.29.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar also drifted within one percent of last week's 11-year lows against sterling, hovering at around $1.8430/35 to the pound.  \par \par \uc2 G7 IN FOCUS  \par \par \uc2 With two weeks to go before the G7 meeting in Boca Raton, Florida, the market's focus was on whether Europe's growing concern about the euro's 20-percent rise over the last year and Japan's worries about a higher yen would result in any changes to the group's attitude on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki told a news conference he hoped to give an accurate picture of Japan's fiscal and monetary policies at the G7 meeting.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its monthly bulletin that it was worried about large exchange rate swings.  \par \par \uc2 ECB Chief Economist Otmar Issing also reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's concern about sharp movements in the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "We hold with our concern about the brutality" of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, he told reporters before addressing a dinner discussing global economic convergence sponsored by the World Economic Forum annual meeting in Davos, Switzerland. ($1=106.05 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040123e01n0006d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
