\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar weaker vs majors on pre-G7 jitters.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2004\par 04:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 22 (Reuters) - The dollar fell on Thursday on growing doubts Group of Seven (G7) finance leaders will take a stand against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness and as the market refocused on the persistent U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 European officials' concerns about the euro's rise were no longer having the sort of impact they did last week, when the dollar bounced by nearly five percent, leaving the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back within sight of life lows.  \par \par \uc2 "European officials are complaining about the euro's rally, but I really think those complaints are also against \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Kota Kimura, assistant manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "European officials must be furious that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is actually exaggerating the euro's rise, since dollar-strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly puts upward pressure on the euro."  \par \par \uc2 Kimura said that as a result, policymakers from the G7 industrial countries nations were unlikely to express a concerted view on the dollar's weakness at their meeting in Florida on February 6-7.  \par \par \uc2 Japan sold a record 20 trillion yen ($187.2 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year and market players estimate it has already offloaded another six trillion in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials have given no sign of easing up on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is employed to sap the export-crimping strength of the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Zembei Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters on Thursday that the Japanese authorities were ready to step in and take action if \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates overshoot. The euro has moved wildly against the dollar, dipping to a one-month low of $1.2350 late last week, before coming back to around $1.2670 by 0250 GMT. That is within two percent of its life highs near $1.29 set last week.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was also weaker against the yen at around 106.90 yen barely one percent off last week's three-year lows around 105.70 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the perception was growing that the dollar's rebound from last week's record lows against the euro had run its course, and the market was now refocusing on problems with U.S. fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 "From a long-term perspective, nothing has really changed in terms of the U.S. current account deficit or expectations that the dollar will eventually head lower," said Hideaki Furumaya, head of the interbank desk at Trust & Custody Services Bank. LUNAR NEW YEAR  \par \par \uc2 Traders said many market participants in Asia were off for the lunar New Year holidays, keeping the market relatively thin and volatile.  \par \par \uc2 The market was awaiting a flurry of public appearances by European and U.S. policymakers including European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) President Jean-Claude Trichet and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's chief economist, Otmar Issing. Both were due to speak at the annual World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, business group Eurochambres said in a statement that Trichet had repeated his concern about excessive swings in the euro's exchange rate at a meeting earlier this week with the group's president, Christoph Leitl. ECB council member and Austrian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Klaus Liebscher said on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an option for central banks but that it would never be discussed beforehand.  \par \par \uc2 But the market impact of such remarks was watered down by comments by other ECB officials who appeared less concerned about the euro's rise.  \par \par \uc2 ECB Governing Council member Nout Wellink was quoted by a news agency on Wednesday as saying that the euro's external value was not excessive and that there was no need to take special measures at the upcoming G7 meeting. ($1=106.86 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040122e01m001gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
