\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Accts Indicate Treasury Buying From MOF Of About Y5T  \b0\par\par\uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2004\par 07:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A sharp rise in repurchase agreement assets held by the Bank of Japan, according to data issued Thursday, indicates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought about Y5 trillion of Treasurys from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far in January.  \par \par \uc2 The amount is in line with speculation and local media reports last week.  \par \par \uc2 The purchases follow a temporary agreement between the MOF and the BOJ set in late December for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the U.S. securities through repurchase agreements to provide the ministry with temporary yen funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 BOJ data on its accounts as of Jan. 20 show that it held Y10.672 trillion of receivables under resale agreements, up Y4.615 trillion from Jan. 10.  \par \par \uc2 "The rise matches about Y5 trillion which markets speculated the BOJ had bought from the ministry," said Izuru Kato, chief economist at Totan Research.  \par \par \uc2 The line item within the accounts usually includes Japanese government bonds and commercial paper that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought via repos as part of its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The outstanding amount from these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely fell by around Y400 billion during the latest 10-day period, according to Kato, leaving roughly Y5 trillion accounted for by the BOJ's buying of Treasurys from the MOF.  \par \par \uc2 The purchase was a half of the Y10 trillion that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was willing to lend the MOF through the repos.  \par \par \uc2 The temporary measure, which the BOJ agreed to take until March, provides the MOF with yen funds until Parliament approves an increase in the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds to Y100 trillion this fiscal year, and to Y140 trillion next fiscal year. An ordinary session of Parliament began Monday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets earlier this month to stem the dollar's fall below Y106. It touched a low of Y105.71. At 0537 GMT, it was quoted at Y106.83.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants speculated that the first of the Treasury repos was conducted last week, although neither government or BOJ officials have confirmed the exact figure.  \par \par \uc2 Should the MOF sell more U.S. securities to the BOJ, the component of the BOJ's assets would rise further in coming months.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, the deposits of the government in the BOJ's accounts declined to Y4.419 trillion Jan. 20 from Y7.418 trillion on Jan. 10, despite the BOJ's Treasury purchases.  \par \par \uc2 Money that BOJ pays to the government for the Treasurys purchases is expected to be shown as an increase in the deposits of the government within the BOJ's accounts, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 But the discrepancy indicates that the MOF redeemed existing financing bills that the BOJ directly underwrites from the government, and made room for future financing bill issuance to the market, Kato added.  \par \par \uc2 -By Michiyo Seki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; michiyo.seki@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040122e01m0003k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*