\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Slips As Top Japan Officials Discuss G7  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 830 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2004\par 06:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar slipped against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in holiday-thinned Asia trading Thursday, as Japan's finance minister and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor met to discuss next month's Group of Seven meeting, a focus of increasingly intense speculation in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki told reporters that he spoke "generally" with Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui about Japan's policy stance ahead of the G7 talks.  \par \par \uc2 "Governor Fukui has had experience" at G7 meetings, Tanigaki said. "It's my first time, so I asked for his support."  \par \par \uc2 He declined to give further details of his discussion with Fukui, an indication of Tokyo's delicate position on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the G7 talks.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation among \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players has grown over how finance ministers and central bankers from the world's seven richest countries will address the dollar's steady slide at talks in Boca Raton, Florida Feb. 6-7.  \par \par \uc2 Japan will have to tread carefully at the meeting, as recent remarks from a number of European officials have suggested they want Asian countries to bear more of the burden of the dollar's decline.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the Finance Ministry wants greater cooperation with the BOJ in part to deflect criticism over its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent more than Y20 trillion last year to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising and hurting exports, and is believed to have sold trillions more this month.  \par \par \uc2 Pressure from the ministry may explain the BOJ's decision to loosen monetary policy this week, upping the target for its quantitative-easing ceiling by Y3 trillion in a move that shows Tokyo isn't relying on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy alone to ensure the economy stages a firm recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "They're trying to show that the government and the BOJ are working together," said Masamichi Koike, head spot dealer at Sumitomo-Mitsui Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Asian markets, thinned by the Lunar New Year holiday, didn't react to the meeting or to much else Thursday, and the dollar moved in relatively tight ranges against its major counterparts. Most markets outside Japan were shut for the traditional holiday.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y106.82, below Y106.92 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y107.13 late Wednesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2672, up from $1.2623 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2617 in Tokyo Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y135.43, up from Y135.07 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y135.19 in Tokyo late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8333, up from $1.8297 in New York and $1.8226 in Tokyo Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's paralysis against the yen also reflects the balance of upside and downside risks for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair ahead of the G7 meeting.  \par \par \uc2 If they play their cards right, Tanigaki and Fukui might be able to harness European officials' recent discontent with the euro's sharp rise to initiate coordinated resistance to the dollar's across-the-board decline.  \par \par \uc2 But they could just as easily wilt under European pressure to give up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Tohru Sasaki, a strategist at JP Morgan.  \par \par \uc2 "Historically, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's MOF has had a tendency to halt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at least temporarily, under gaiatsu, or heightened foreign pressure," he says, drawing a parallel with last September's G7 meeting in Dubai, when the group called for more-flexible exchange rates and Tokyo pulled out of the market for several weeks.  \par \par \uc2 "Therefore, we see a good chance that (the dollar) will fall below Y105 around the next G7, just as the Y115 level fell going into the Dubai meeting," he says.  \par \par \uc2 SMBC's Koike said the prospects of coordinated action to stem the dollar's fall are virtually nil.  \par \par \uc2 "They can't do anything unless the U.S. gives consent," something that's unlikely to happen. "The U.S. has no problem at all" with the dollar's decline.  \par \par \uc2 He says the euro is likely to continue gathering strength against the dollar through the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 But Koike is also skeptical that euro-zone G7 members will succeed in arm-twisting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  into giving up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "There was a push last time (in Dubai) to even out global imbalances - that's what 'flexibility' was all about," he says. "I think we'll se a repetition of that language, but nothing more."  \par \par \uc2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040122e01m00030\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
