\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  BOJ Easing May Lift Yen If Japan Stks Gain  \b0\par\par\uc2 448 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2004\par 08:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 In its easing move, the BOJ boosted its target for banks' account balances at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Y3 trillion, seemingly with a goal to sap the yen's strength, but the step also risks boosting the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further, Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase Bank in Tokyo, said in a report.  \par \par \uc2 "Because the policy is unlikely to lead to a change in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, its effect on the dollar/yen is probably limited. But if the monetary easing results in rises in Japanese stock prices, then that could lead to a stronger yen," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Commerzbank's Muramatsu said that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's near-term direction depends on whether it can break above Y107.50 in days ahead.  \par \par \uc2 "Say, tomorrow, if the dollar again sinks into the Y106s, it would settle back into a recent range between Y105 and Y107.50," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The odds of the dollar rising past Y107.50 appear low, given talk among Tokyo traders and brokers that Japanese exporters will gear up their dollar sales in the mid-107s.  \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled about 70 pips against the dollar in late Asian trade Wednesday after peaking near $1.2627 on buying by Asian names, a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Thin liquidity was a major culprit behind the sharp movements, a Japanese trader said. Earlier Wednesday, Mizuho's Karitani noted Asia's euro market had "only one-hundredth of the liquidity observed overseas yesterday."  \par \par \uc2 The euro's fall quickly ended near $1.2550, where a Tokyo trader said "thick" buying orders were lying in wait.  \par \par \uc2 Commerzbank's Muramatsu voiced doubts over European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Otmar Issing's remarks Tuesday that recent "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " had helped weaken the euro against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 When ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet said early last week he was worried about the euro's sharp moves, "it surely did surprise the market as few players had expected it" and led the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower, Muramatsu said.  \par \par \uc2 "But the market has realized economic fundamentals are unchanged, and so are the potential of the euro's rise and the dollar's fall," he said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040121e01l0007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
