\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Up Vs Yen On Position Adjustments Pre-G7  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 862 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2004\par 06:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar advanced slightly against the yen in Asia Wednesday as players adjusted positions ahead of the upcoming meeting of finance officials from the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback began ascending in early Asian trade after dipping below Y107, as U.S. and European hedge funds covered dollar short-positions, probably in preparation for the G7 meeting in Florida Feb. 6-7, Tokyo traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar eventually settled into a tight range between Y107.10 and Y107.25, with the yen-bearish effect of the Bank of Japan's policy easing Tuesday wilting away.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ's action was basically a non-event, said Ryohei Muramatsu, manager of treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Commerzbank's Tokyo branch. "The three major dollar-bearish elements - the U.S. current account and budget deficits, low U.S. interest rates and terrorism concerns - remain deep-seated" and will continue to weigh on the dollar, he said.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. President George Bush's State of Union speech, which came around midmorning Tokyo time, didn't ruffle the dollar, although his call for permanent tax cuts indicated that the U.S. deficits won't be narrowing anytime soon, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell against the euro, with traders saying recent verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from European policy makers over the past two days was less aggressive than the market had anticipated.  \par \par \uc2 Monday's statements from European Union finance ministers, or Ecofin, "showed that their level of concern over the euro's appreciation wasn't as strong as the market had expected," said Tatsuro Karitani, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division at Mizuho Corporate Bank. "The market had priced in those expectations too much."  \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped to around $1.2625 in the afternoon as buy-stop orders were triggered when the euro neared $1.2590.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y107.13, above Y107.05 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y107.11 late Tuesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2617, higher than $1.2580 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2456 in Tokyo Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y135.19, up from Y134.65 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y132.43 in Tokyo late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8226, up from $1.8205 in New York and higher than $1.7918 in Tokyo Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 In its easing move, the BOJ boosted its target for banks' account balances at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Y3 trillion, seemingly with a goal to sap the yen's strength, but the step also risks boosting the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further, Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase Bank in Tokyo, said in a report.  \par \par \uc2 "Because the policy is unlikely to lead to a change in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, its effect on the dollar/yen is probably limited. But if the monetary easing results in rises in Japanese stock prices, then that could lead to a stronger yen," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Commerzbank's Muramatsu said that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's near-term direction depends on whether it can break above Y107.50 in days ahead.  \par \par \uc2 "Say, tomorrow, if the dollar again sinks into the Y106s, it would settle back into a recent range between Y105 and Y107.50," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The odds of the dollar rising past Y107.50 appear low, given talk among Tokyo traders and brokers that Japanese exporters will gear up their dollar sales in the mid-107s.  \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled about 70 pips against the dollar in late Asian trade Wednesday after peaking near $1.2627 on buying by Asian names, a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Thin liquidity was a major culprit behind the sharp movements, a Japanese trader said. Earlier Wednesday, Mizuho's Karitani noted Asia's euro market had "only one-hundredth of the liquidity observed overseas yesterday."  \par \par \uc2 The euro's fall quickly ended near $1.2550, where a Tokyo trader said "thick" buying orders were lying in wait.  \par \par \uc2 Commerzbank's Muramatsu voiced doubts over European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Otmar Issing's remarks Tuesday that recent "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " had helped weaken the euro against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 When ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet said early last week he was worried about the euro's sharp moves, "it surely did surprise the market as few players had expected it" and led the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower, Muramatsu said.  \par \par \uc2 "But the market has realized economic fundamentals are unchanged, and so are the potential of the euro's rise and the dollar's fall," he said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040121e01l0004b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
