\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro surges, eurogroup comments seen as buy signal.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2004\par 13:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 20 (Reuters) - The euro rose 1.5 percent against the yen and more than one percent versus the dollar on Tuesday, as investors treated the lack of concrete details from a eurogroup meeting the previous session as a green light to buy.  \par \par \uc2 A statement after a meeting of euro zone finance ministers and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late on Monday avoided the usual wording of wanting a strong and stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stressing instead discontent about the pace of euro gains after it hit record highs near $1.29 last week.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts noted, however, the policymakers did not discuss contingency plans for tackling any renewed euro volatility and said this, coupled with technical trading influences, lit a rocket under the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "It's technical positioning after the dollar index failed at 88, and there was really nothing new out of the eurogroup meeting - we need a stronger definition of excessive volatility and what they are going to do about it," said Trevor Dinmore, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2 The euro broke back above $1.25 to trade at its highest since Friday at $1.2533 by 1230 GMT, regaining two cents of its losses of more than five cents over the past week, and on course for its largest one-day gain since November.  \par \par \uc2 It also hit its highest in more than a week against the yen at 134.87 yen .   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar fell to 87.08 against an index of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   after hitting\par a one-month high earlier just shy of 88. The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also lost\par more than one percent against the pound       , the Swiss franc\par and the Australian dollar       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro suffered only brief losses earlier in the European session after Hans-Werner Sinn, head of Germany's Ifo institute, said the ECB should \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to bring the euro below $1.20, comments made after Germany's ZEW expectations indicator eased in January.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are in choppy trading conditions, but we have established a market that is far more evenly balanced in terms of flows - the dollar is no longer a one-way bet," said Derek Halpenny, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOJ MOVE  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fared better against the yen, hitting two-week highs of 107.73 , after the BOJ made a surprise easing in monetary policy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ raised excess liquidity in the banking system - as measured by banks' current account deposits held at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - to 30-35 trillion yen ($280-326 billion) from 27-32 trillion, a move read by markets as a sign of concern about export-damaging yen strength.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan spent a record 20 trillion yen to prevent the yen rising last year and is thought to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily since the start of this year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Toshihiko Fukui said in late Tokyo trade moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market could become a risk for the Japanese economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 G7 FOCUS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With a key Group of Seven finance ministers' meeting now just over two weeks away, analysts said policymakers in the euro zone and Japan were preparing their positions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's significant (the Europeans) pulled together and got a cohesive view. It's more in harmony to be saying they don't like volatility," said Paul Mackel, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French Finance Minister Francis Mer said on Tuesday the euro zone statement was a basis for the Florida G7 on February 6-7, but declined to venture an estimate of a suitable euro/dollar level.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He also said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stability "is a dream" but maybe there were limits not to be passed.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market gets another opportunity to assess Europe's stance and gauge how close the ECB may be to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets when ECB chief economist Otmar Issing testifies before a European parliamentary committee at 1400 GMT.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There is little U.S. data on the agenda for Tuesday. The biggest U.S. event is U.S. President George W. Bush's State of the Union speech later in the day.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040120e01k002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
