\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yo-yoing euro recovers one percent vs dollar.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 703 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2004\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 20 (Reuters) - The euro rose one percent against the dollar on Tuesday, clawing back some of its heavy losses of the past few days, while the yen hit a two-week low on the dollar after a surprise easing by the Bank of Japan.  \par \par \uc2 A statement by euro zone finance ministers and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meeting late on Monday, avoided the usual wording of wanting a strong and stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stressing instead their discontent about the pace of euro gains after it hit record highs near $1.29 last week.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts noted, however, they did not discuss contingency plans for tackling any renewed euro volatility and said this gap, coupled with technical trading influences, was helping to lift the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ raised excess liquidity in the banking system - as measured by banks' current account deposits held at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - to 30-35 trillion yen ($280-326 billion) from 27-32 trillion, a move read by markets as a sign of concern about export-damaging yen strength.  \par \par \uc2 "Today's euro buying is a reflection of the fact that Japan is showing no intent to let the yen strengthen, so markets are left with the euro as next best thing," said Tim Fox, market strategist at National Australia Bank in London.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rose as far as $1.2492, 1-1/2 cents above one-month lows set on Monday. It had shed over five cents in a week after hitting the record peak last week.  \par \par \uc2 But the euro fell back to $1.2444 by 1050 GMT after Hans-Werner Sinn, head of Germany's Ifo institute, said the ECB should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring the euro below $1.20.  \par \par \uc2 Also weighing on the euro was a slight weakening in Germany's ZEW expectation's indicator, which fell to 72.9 in January from 73.4 in December.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rallied more than one percent on the day to 134 yen, while sterling and the Australian dollar also rose one percent on the day against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We are in choppy trading conditions, but we have established a market that is far more evenly balanced in terms of flows - the dollar is no longer a one-way bet," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was at 107.61 yen, off earlier highs around 107.70 and nearly two yen above a three-year low set earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said in late Tokyo trade moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market could become a risk for the Japanese economy.  \par \par \uc2 G7 IN SIGHT  \par \par \uc2 With a key Group of Seven finance ministers' meeting now just over two weeks away, analysts said policymakers in the euro zone and Japan were preparing their positions.  \par \par \uc2 "It's significant (the Europeans) pulled together and got a cohesive view. It's more in harmony to be saying they don't like volatility," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro in London.  \par \par \uc2 The market gets another opportunity to assess Europe's stance and gauge how close the ECB may be to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when ECB chief economist Otmar Issing testifies before a European parliamentary committee at 1400 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 SCEPTICISM OVER BOJ  \par \par \uc2 In Japan, where interest rates are already close to zero, the BOJ's quantitative easing, ostensibly to try to boost the economy, was viewed with scepticism with analysts saying the move was related to recent Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen gains.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record 20 trillion yen to prevent the yen rising last year and is thought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily since the start of this year.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the decision was prompted by the strong yen, and there were two main factors - its impact on the economy, and the difficulty of money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  caused by massive amounts of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Kiichi Murashima, economic and market analysis director at Nikko Citigroup in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 There is little U.S. data on the agenda for Tuesday. The biggest U.S. event is U.S. President George W. Bush's State of the Union speech later in the day.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040120e01k001yq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
