\par\par \b \uc2 WRAP: BOJ Surprises With Easing To Keep Econ On Track  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Iain McDonald  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 760 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2004\par 06:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday eased monetary policy in a surprise move to maintain the country's economic revival and overcome deflation, after the yen's recent rise threatened to knock the recovery off course.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan's nine-member board voted by a majority to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's liquidity target by Y3 trillion to a new range of Y30 trillion to Y35 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the extra cash gives the BOJ more flexibility to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's campaign to stop the yen from rising against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Despite recent data indicating economic activity continues to accelerate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the looser monetary conditions aim to "ensure an economic recovery and to show our stance of beating deflation."  \par \par \uc2 Persistent structural problems in Japan mean the pace of recovery will stay moderate and consumer prices will maintain a gradual decline, it said.  \par \par \uc2 "In the meantime, developments in financial and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and their impact warrant close monitoring," the BOJ said.  \par \par \uc2 That last sentence is a clear signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is targeting the yen in its latest policy action, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 The easing is "to prevent the yen from rising and to support the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Masaaki Kanno, managing director of economic research at J.P. Morgan in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      BOJ, Govt In Concert \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen has risen nearly 11% against the dollar since the beginning of last August. In response, Tokyo sold a record Y20.05 trillion in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last year and is believed to have already sold several trillion more this month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A boost to liquidity indicates the BOJ wants to be seen as working in concert with the government, not only in halting the yen's rise, but also in defeating deflation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That's despite the fact that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has indicated in the past that throwing more cash at the economy won't solve the structural problems.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The BOJ wants to show that it's on the same page as the government and that there's no rift between the two," says Koichi Ono, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  economist at Daiwa Institute of Research.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By boosting the target for liquidity, which the BOJ measures through commercial banks' account balances at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can engage in more yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  without having to drain yen from domestic money markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Selling yen in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market without offsetting draining \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pushes up banks' account balances.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kanno said the BOJ, in its latest action, wants to take advantage of foreign investor perceptions that unsterilized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is more effective than sterilized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held steady its targeted monthly outright purchases of Japanese government bonds at Y1.2 trillion.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The easing had a limited impact on financial markets. The dollar popped up to Y107.62 from around 107.50 just before the announcement while 10-year JGB futures rose to 138.56 from 138.45. Stock prices held onto earlier gains.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0520 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y107.51, JGB futures were at 138.44 and the Nikkei 225 Stock Index was up 1.15% at 11163.66.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      Eases ABS Buying Rules \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Separately, the BOJ board decided to ease its rules for asset-backed securities buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  launched last year in an effort to make finance more readily available to smaller firms.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market participants have said that the rules were too tight and so far the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has bought only a limited amount of securities under the plan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ said it would now accept asset-backed commercial paper that has assigned to it a credit rating from just one agency. Previously, eligible ABCP had to have two or more credit ratings.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It also watered down the rule the ratio of underlying assets related to smaller firms be 50%. It said that ratio could be calculated either on a value or number of individual assets. Previously it had said the calculation should be based on value only.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also said that it has changed the dates of its next policy meeting to Feb. 4-5 from Feb. 5-6 as the initial schedule conflicted with a Group of Seven meeting of finance ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governors on Feb. 6-7.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Iain McDonald, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2941; iain.mcdonald@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Hiroshi Inoue, Michiyo Seki and Miyako Takebe contributed to this article).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040120e01k0004l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
