\par\par \b \uc2 Europe, Japan Step Up Calls For  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Stability Ahead Of G7  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Adriana Arai  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2004\par 16:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The euro zone and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  are stepping up verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb their surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, signaling a preference for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability over flexibility as the U.S. dollar weakens.  \par \par \uc2 Policymakers from the 12 nations that use the euro changed their policy stance late Monday, by stating the euro "must keep its value over the medium and long run, in line with economic fundamentals. In the present circumstances, we particularly stress stability and we are concerned about excessive exchange-rate moves."  \par \par \uc2 A few hours later, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took markets by surprise by easing monetary policy, despite growing signals that the economy is emerging from a decade-long economic slump. The decision, authorities said, was a response to the yen's appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 The moves put the euro zone and Japan on a collision course with the U.S. less than three weeks before policymakers from the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations meet in Florida on Feb. 6-7. The event is expected to be dominated by a debate over the value of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and their impact on the global economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say their message is clear: Europe and Japan will pressure the U.S. to change the G7 stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies, after a September statement urging more flexibility caused both the euro and the yen to rise by roughly 7% versus the dollar on a trade-weighted basis.  \par \par \uc2 "It's quite clear Europe and Japan are unhappy with the extent of the appreciation of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the last G7 meeting," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist with Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London. "The speculation now is that they're looking for a change in the G7 statement, indicating a desire for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability, which is exactly the opposite of the statement" issued in September after the G7 meeting in Dubai.  \par \par \uc2 Back then, investors interpreted the G7 call for flexibility as targeted at Japan and piled on the yen, sending it sharply stronger. The dollar fell nearly Y5 to below Y110 in two weeks before Japanese authorities resumed aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a further decline. Then investors started buying the euro again.  \par \par \uc2 Despite Japanese buying of dollars, the yen has gradually risen since and the dollar is now around mid-Y107.00. The euro has risen to mid-$1.2500 from around $1.12 in the same period.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par        US Unlikely To Bow To New Pressure \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chances that European and Japanese officials will succeed in persuading their U.S. counterparts at the February G7 meeting are very slim, though. Analysts say the U.S. is benefiting from a weakening dollar, which is boosting corporate earnings by making U.S. exports more competitive and aiding a recovery in a presidential election year. So there would be no incentive to change.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even Federal Reserve Bank officials seem comfortable with the dollar's fall. They recently stated the dollar's depreciation has been orderly and poises no risk to the inflation outlook.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback is now at its weakest level in more than six years on a trade-weighted basis, an adjustment economists and officials say was needed to narrow a large U.S. current-account deficit that could potentially pose a threat to the global economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's too early to see G7 officials move away from their stance hammered out in Dubai," said Aziz McMahon, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with ABN Amro in London. "Any change could cause the dollar to rally quite a lot and that wouldn't be good for what has been weak job creation in an election year."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While investors await the next G7 statement on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, Halpenny said trading in the world's top three \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isexpected to stay choppy and players are unlikely to add large positions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tuesday, the euro was trading higher despite the statement from European ministers. Traders said the declaration had no impact on the market because it merely made official a variety of isolated policymakers' comments trying to talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down last week. The Bank of Japan's move to ease monetary policy, because unexpected, had a bigger impact on the yen, sending it lower.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the yen could weaken a bit more going into the G7 meeting because Japanese authorities have signaled they're ready to use policy tools other than outright \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from rising.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Around 1430 GMT, the euro was changing hands at $1.2517, up from $1.2347 late Monday in North America but down from a record high of $1.2900 last Monday. The dollar was stronger at Y107.60 from Y107.22.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires, 44 207 842 9483 adriana.arai@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCS000020040120e01k0008n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
