\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar steady vs majors on capital inflows data.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara   \par \uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2004\par 07:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 19 (Reuters) - The dollar kept most of its recent gains against major rivals on Monday on improved sentiment due to steady capital inflows to U.S. assets and as the market mulled what might emerge from the upcoming Group of Seven (G7) meeting.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar notched its biggest one-day rise versus the euro in five months on Friday, when it climbed as high as $1.2350 - a level not seen in a month. By 0256 GMT, it was standing at $1.2370/75 per euro.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the market took heart from data showing that net foreign purchases of U.S. assets tripled to $87.6 billion in November from the previous month.   \par \par \uc2 "Steady inflows to U.S. assets means less worries about the United States not being able to finance its massive current account deficit, which has been a major factor battering the dollar," said Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.   \par \par \uc2 "That took some pressure off the dollar, especially as euro-zone officials have repeatedly voiced concerns about the euro's rapid rise versus the dollar."   \par \par \uc2 Among the latest remarks, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Economist Otmar Issing said on Friday that the ECB was not indifferent to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.   \par \par \uc2 After Issing, ECB council member Guy Quaden said a further rise in the euro was not desirable.   \par \par \uc2 Amid the recent barrage of coments from euro-zone officials, the market is focused on how G7 policy-makers will react to the overall dollar's weakness at their meeting in Florida on February 6-7.   \par \par \uc2 Views are divided, with many market participants believing that U.S. officials are satisfied with the dollar's weakness since it helps U.S. manufacturers.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow reiterating on Friday the Bush administration's strong dollar policy and that markets should set \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.   \par \par \uc2 Many dealers were focusing on a meeting of euro-zone finance ministers at 1800 GMT, with any comments on euro strength likely to be closely watched.   \par \par \uc2 But trading was expected to be thin due to the U.S. holiday in honour of Martin Luther King Jr.   \par \par \uc2 PRESSURE ON YEN TO RISE   \par \par \uc2 The dollar was a tad weaker against the yen, trading at 106.51/54 yen versus 106.63/71 in late U.S. trade.   \par \par \uc2 Although some traders said the dollar's rise against the yen could be capped on expected selling by Japanese exporters, dollar bulls said short-covering was likely, given the huge yen-long positions taken by speculators.   \par \par \uc2 Data from the Commodity Futures Trading Commission showed on Friday that yen futures speculators extended net long positions to 60,602 contracts in the week that ended on January 13 from 56,834 contracts a week earlier.   \par \par \uc2 But over the longer term, analysts said there would be few factors pushing down the yen except \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's capital flows data show Japanese investors are still buying foreign bonds. But this has not lead to a higher yen as most of the purchases are fully hedged, and foreign investors keep buying Japanese stocks," said Tomoko Fujii, market and economic analysis director at Nikko Citigroup in Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2 "Some investors seem to have already started repatriating their overseas investments, so further upward pressure on the yen is likely to continue," she said.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040119e01j000md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
