\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar recovers, buoyed by strong data.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2004\par 16:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment, changes byline, dateline; previous LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 16 (Reuters) - The dollar rose steeply against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, boosted by robust economic data that seemed to confirm a more vigorous U.S. recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Net foreign purchases of U.S. assets jumped to $87.6 billion in November, sharply higher than a revised $27.8 billion in October.  \par \par \uc2 "Total (dollar) positive reaction to the flows data. It was almost instantaneous. The private accounts showed a big turnaround," said Grant Wilson, vice president at Mellon Bank in Pittsburgh.  \par \par \uc2 "This more than than covers the huge (current account) deficit that we run because this is such a huge number. This is very, very dollar positive," he said.  \par \par \uc2 By midmorning New York trade, the euro was trading at $1.2432, off more than 1 percent, and close to 5 cents from Monday's record highs around $1.29. The euro fell more than 1 percent against the yen to 131.76, near the day's low.  \par \par \uc2 But the dollar was 0.3 percent down at 106.01 yen, having hit a low around 105.70 before being turned back by suspected Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the dollar rose over 1 percent to 1.2608 francs. Sterling fell to $1.8056, off 0.8 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 Even a lower than expected increase in U.S. industrial production did not dent the dollar's rally. Industrial production rose a 0.1 percent, while the percentage of firms' capacity in use was steady at 75.8 percent.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. business inventories rose 0.3 percent in November after a 0.4 percent increase the previous month, indicating a pickup in economic activity.  \par \par \uc2 A University of Michigan preliminary survey on consumer sentiment came in at 103.2 in January, compared with December's final reading of 92.6. The median forecast had called for 94.0. This was the highest reading since November 2002.  \par \par \uc2 "That figure certainly helps the ECB's (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) cause, and they wouldn't mind a rapid fall in the euro. They're sitting there and saying 'Keep going, keep going'," said Brian Taylor, head \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Manufacturers and Traders Bank.  \par \par \uc2 EUROPEAN COMMENTS  \par \par \uc2 This week's barrage of comments from euro zone officials expressing concern about the surging single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed no signs of abating on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 ECB chief economist Otmar Issing launched Friday's offensive, which added to downward pressure on the euro, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not indifferent to the euro's strength.  \par \par \uc2 Issing's comments and those of other European officials this week fueled speculation that the ECB could cut rates at its next meeting in February to stem the euro's climb, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "There's a sudden shift in attitude in the sense that there is greater acceptance that the dollar is going to have a correction partly because of what may or may not happen at the G7 meeting," said Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Group Ltd in Chicago.  \par \par \uc2 Central bankers and finance ministers of the world's seven major industrialized nations are due to meet in early February in Florida.  \par \par \uc2 "My bias is nothing on the macro backdrop has changed for the dollar that much. This a question of how much we can run at the threat of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or an ECB rate cut," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040116e01g002tj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
