\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro falls further, BoJ seen pushing yen off highs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2004\par 12:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 16 (Reuters) - The euro's losses snowballed on Friday, boosting the yen and prompting the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hit three-year highs against the dollar before being turned back by suspected Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BoJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 This week's barrage of comments from euro zone officials expressing concern about the euro's 20 percent rise on the dollar over the past year showed no signs of abating on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) chief economist Otmar Issing was the latest official to say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not indifferent to the euro's strength, adding to pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall.  \par \par \uc2 "It is a euro story now," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez in London.  \par \par \uc2 "Issing had added to comments we have already heard from (ECB President Jean-Claude) Trichet, (ECB council member Christian) Noyer and (Bundesbank President Ernst) Welteke."  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, suspected BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have also reminded the market Japan is unhappy with export-damaging yen strength.  \par \par \uc2 By 1100 GMT, the euro was trading near the day's low around 132.44 yen, down nearly one percent on the day. It was also at $1.2500, off about 0.6 percent, and down roughly four cents from Monday's record highs around $1.2900.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was 0.5 percent down on the day at 105.89 having hit a low around 105.70 before suspected BoJ action pulled it higher.  \par \par \uc2 There was no official confirmation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 EUROPEAN OFFENSIVE CONTINUES  \par \par \uc2 Issing reiterated comments from ECB President Trichet saying that Trichet had shown "we are not indifferent about the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate but worried over the large volatility".  \par \par \uc2 However, Issing also told reporters before addressing an economic symposium that the euro was not to blame for Germany's poor economic performance last year.  \par \par \uc2 He said a strong euro would offset some of the inflationary impact caused by higher taxes and administered prices that are expected to push euro zone inflation higher in the first quarter of 2004.  \par \par \uc2 The market's main focus remains on how policymakers from the Group of Seven industrial countries will react to the dollar's weakness at the meeting in Florida on February 6-7.  \par \par \uc2 G7 deputy finance ministers from each country are meeting in Brussels on January 26 to work on the agenda for the February meeting.  \par \par \uc2 But apparent nonchalance about the dollar's fall on the U.S. side has fanned expectations Washington is comfortable with a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 This view was highlighted by Japanese trade minister Shoichi Nakagawa who said he thought U.S. authorities did not really want a strong dollar despite Washington's official stance to the contrary.  \par \par \uc2 "A lot of profit taking on positioning is going on because the euro has come long way and the (euro zone officials') rhetoric is helping. There is still demand to buy yen and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mary Davis, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at CSFB in London.  \par \par \uc2 "The gap in monetary policy management in the U.S. and the euro zone will persist. The net result is that the dollar's recovery is unlikely to go that far."  \par \par \uc2 Later on Friday, the U.S. releases data on industrial production and a University of Michigan consumer sentiment survey.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN IS VIGILANT  \par \par \uc2 A source from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said there was no change in its stance to act appropriately on excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.  \par \par \uc2 This followed comments from Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki earlier, who reiterated that Tokyo would take decisive action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to counter any overshooting in exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts noted the dollar had recovered ground against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like sterling and the Australian dollar in recent days but had made almost no progress against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "For one thing, the decline in recent months against the yen had been relatively small because of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In addition, there is concern that such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come under criticism at the upcoming G7 meeting," said Masamichi Koike, head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Bank in Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040116e01g0027v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
