\par\par \b \uc2 Euro steady as EU officials fret over rapid rise.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Naomi Tajitsu  \par \uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2004\par 07:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 15 (Reuters) - The euro was trading in tight ranges on Thursday after complaints from European officials about its strength against the dollar took some air out of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upward momentum.   \par \par \uc2  European officials have stepped up their rhetoric this week on the euro, making traders cautious about pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher ahead of a meeting of economic policy makers from the Group of Seven (G7) industrial countries next month.   \par \par \uc2  Smaller-than-expected U.S. trade deficit figures on Wednesday also helped to support the dollar, traders said.   \par \par \uc2  "Things have changed quite a bit this week. The spectre of the G7 coming out with something is keeping people on their toes," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of international bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Daiwa Securities SMBC.   \par \par \uc2  G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors meet in Florida on February 6-7, and the dollar's broad-based weakness is widely expected to be a major topic.   \par \par \uc2  Although the market was relatively quiet on Thursday, dealers said the euro's movements against the dollar could fluctuate either way in the lead-up to the meeting.   \par \par \uc2  "If the euro goes back up to $1.27, the market could turn bullish, if it goes down to $1.25, it could turn bearish," said Toshihiro Azuma, a manager at Sumitomo Trust and Banking.   \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, traders pointed out that the dollar's mild turnaround has mainly been due to repositioning and reflected a gearing down in the speed of the euro's rise. They added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downtrend was set to continue for some time.   \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  council member Christian Noyer became the latest official to express concerns about the euro's appreciation this week, saying on Wednesday that monetary authorities remained vigilant about the euro's level.   \par \par \uc2  At 0620 GMT, the euro was at $1.2663/66 about two percent below the record high near $1.29 hit earlier in the week and up a tad from $1.2645 late on Wednesday in New York.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  JITTERS   \par \par \uc2  The dollar was steady against the yen, hovering around 106.20 yen   \par \par \uc2  Although it dipped slightly under 106 yen on Wednesday, coming within sight of three-year lows around 105.90 set last week, traders said the dollar was underpinned by wariness of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to come under pressure from its peers over its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy when the G7 meets.   \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities conducted a record 20 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year and are thought to have spent heavily since the start of this year.   \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki reiterated on Thursday that the dollar's fall was going too far given U.S. economic strength, and that Japan would take appropriate action, as needed, in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2  This view was echoed by Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, who added that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets should be stable and reflect the relative strength of the U.S. economy.   \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen stood at 134.50 yen, slightly up on the day but down sharply from last Friday's peaks around 137.80.   \par \par \uc2  For now, the market was waiting to see if more euro zone officials would join the jawboning foray, with ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet speaking in Naples later in the day.   \par \par \uc2  Traders also awaited U.S. retail sales and consumer prices data for December, due out at 1330 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040115e01f001jy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
